{"The test case \"Should deny on explicit cache deny entry\" is non-diagnostic because it sets the permission cache value to false (equivalent to missing) and uses the default fakeStore with no permissions. The test would still deny even if permDenialCache were not checked, allowing denial-cache regressions to slip through CI.": 0.8965796232223511, "The userPermDenialCacheKey function concatenates name and parent using _ as delimiter, but both components can contain underscores (Grafana UIDs allow a-zA-Z0-9\\-\\_). Different (name, parent) pairs like (\"some_dashboard\", \"fold1\") and (\"some\", \"dashboard_fold1\") produce identical cache keys, causing one resource's denial to falsely deny access to a different resource for up to 30 seconds.": 0.9333570599555969}